blocks.en:
The next interesting question is of course if the index of $\mathcal{A}$ is finite, and more particularly, when it is zero. One of the standard methods in answering this question is to exploit the homotopy invariance of the Fredholm index. Consider for example a second-order elliptic operator
\begin{equation}\label{eq:elliptic-dirichlet-index-homotopy-operator}
L(\bm{x},D)u=a_{ij}(\bm{x})\frac{\partial^2u}{\partial x_i\partial x_j}+b_i(\bm{x})\frac{\partial u}{\partial x_i}+c(\bm{x})u
\end{equation}
with Dirichlet boundary condition $B(\bm{x},D)u=u$. We assume the matrix $a_{ij}$ is symmetric and positive definite. We may then consider the one-parameter family of operators
\begin{equation}\label{eq:elliptic-dirichlet-laplace-homotopy}
L_t=(1-t)\Delta+tL,\quad B_t=B.
\end{equation}

blocks.zh:
下一个有趣的问题当然是 $\mathcal{A}$ 的指标是否有限, 更具体地说, 何时为零. 回答这一问题的标准方法之一是利用 Fredholm 指标的同伦不变性. 例如, 考虑二阶椭圆算子
\begin{equation}\label{eq:elliptic-dirichlet-index-homotopy-operator}
L(\bm{x},D)u=a_{ij}(\bm{x})\frac{\partial^2u}{\partial x_i\partial x_j}+b_i(\bm{x})\frac{\partial u}{\partial x_i}+c(\bm{x})u
\end{equation}
及 Dirichlet 边界条件 $B(\bm{x},D)u=u$. 假设矩阵 $a_{ij}$ 对称且正定. 于是可以考虑算子的单参数族
\begin{equation}\label{eq:elliptic-dirichlet-laplace-homotopy}
L_t=(1-t)\Delta+tL,\quad B_t=B.
\end{equation}
